ame\":\"What\u0027s the difference between an HOA master policy and HO-6?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"The master policy covers association-owned buildings, common areas, and shared liability. HO-6 covers unit owner personal property, interior improvements, personal liability, and loss assessment exposure.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Do condo owners need HO-6 insurance?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"In most cases, yes. The master policy typically does not cover your personal belongings, interior upgrades, or your share of association deductibles and special assessments.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"What should boards review at renewal?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Building valuation, deductible structure, ordinance or law limits, general liability, umbrella, D\u0026O, and crime/fidelity coverage. We prepare a clear summary covering all of these.\"}}]}"},{"url":"/why-choose-us","title":"Why Choose HOA Insurance Agency â€” Specialists in HOA \u0026amp; Condo Insurance","desc":"HOA-only focus, coordinated coverage systems, defensible renewal strategies, and HO-6 programs that reduce board headaches. See why associations choose ProtectMyHOA. Free review â€” 508-233-2261.","canonical":"https://www.protectmyhoa.com/why-choose-us","robots":"","h1":1,"jsonld":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"InsuranceAgency\",\"name\":\"HOA Insurance Agency\",\"url\":\"https://www.protectmyhoa.com\",\"telephone\":\"+1-508-233-2261\",\"email\":\"insurance@ProtectMyHOA.com\",\"address\":{\"@type\":\"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"420 Lakeside Ave, Suite 202\",\"addressLocality\":\"Marlborough\",\"addressRegion\":\"MA\",\"postalCode\":\"01752\",\"addressCountry\":\"US\"},\"areaServed\":[{\"@type\":\"State\",\"name\":\"Massachusetts\"},{\"@type\":\"State\",\"name\":\"Rhode Island\"},{\"@type\":\"State\",\"name\":\"New Hampshire\"},{\"@type\":\"State\",\"name\":\"Connecticut\"},{\